,\n 130          name: t.name,\n 131          definition: toDefinition(`${serverId}__${t.name}`, t),\n```\n\n## E04.4\n\n**Check:** A scanner error or outage blocks the metadata instead of letting it through unchecked.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Read every `try/except`, `catch`, and timeout around the scanner call. 2) Check an error blocks the metadata. 3) Answer no if any error branch passes metadata through, returns clean, or skips the scan, or a config flag disables scanning by default.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:** src/tools/registry.ts:116 — \"metadata scan error\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** A throw from the scanner rejects the whole server (registry.ts:113-118); covered by controls.test.ts:86\n\n`src/tools/registry.ts` lines 104–128 (cited lines marked >):\n```\n 104      meta: ServerMeta,\n 105      invoke: (tool: string, input: Record<string, unknown>, opts: InvokeOptions) => Promise<unknown>,\n 106    ): void {\n 107      const cfg = this.servers.find((s) => s.id === serverId);\n 108      if (!cfg) {\n 109        this.rejected.push({ serverId, reason: `server not in release manifest (reported name ${reportedName ?? \"none\"})` });\n 110        return;\n 111      }\n 112      let scan;\n 113      try {\n 114        scan = scanServer(meta, this.bareNamesExcept(serverId));\n 115      } catch (err) {\n 116>       this.rejected.push({ serverId, reason: `metadata scan error: ${(err as Error).message}` });\n 117        return;\n 118      }\n 119      if (scan.serverRejected) {\n 120        this.rejected.push({ serverId, reason: `server metadata findings: ${JSON.stringify(scan.serverFindings)}` });\n 121        return;\n 122      }\n 123      for (const [tool, findings] of scan.rejectedTools) {\n 124        this.rejected.push({ serverId, tool, reason: `tool metadata findings: ${JSON.stringify(findings)}` });\n 125      }\n 126      for (const t of scan.acceptedTools) {\n 127        this.add({\n 128          key: `${serverId}__${t.name}`,\n```\n\n## Your answer\n\nWrite this JSON to E04.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in verdicts.json under \"E04\"):\n```json\n{\"verdict\": \"upheld | failed | unclear\",\n \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"E04.1\", \"result\": \"holds | fails | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\", \"note\": \"why\"}],\n \"note\": \"one sentence\"}\n```\nVerdict is **failed** if any check fails, **unclear** if none fails but any is unclear, otherwise **upheld**. A failed check needs the quoted line that makes it false: `evidence` is path:line, and `quote` is the exact text of that line. To cite two places, list both refs in `evidence` (`a.py:12, b.yaml:40`) and put each line's text on its own line in `quote`. If the check fails, add `\"violates\": [\"words copied exactly from the requirement\"]`.\nagent\nagent/infra\nagent/infra/terraform\nagent/infra/terraform/main.tf\nagent/infra/terraform/github.tf\nagent/infra/terraform/iam.tf\nagent/test\nagent/test/controls.test.ts\nagent/test/budget.test.ts\nagent/config\nagent/config/tools.allowlist.yaml\nagent/config/policy.yaml\nagent/config/budgets.yaml\nagent/Dockerfile\nagent/k8s\nagent/k8s/deployment.yaml\nagent/release\nagent/release/manifest.json\nagent/README.md\nagent/package.json\nagent/.github\nagent/.github/CODEOWNERS\nagent/.github/workflows\nagent/.github/workflows/deploy.yml\nagent/.github/workflows/ci.yml\nagent/prompts\nagent/prompts/intent-classifier.txt\nagent/prompts/system.md\nagent/tsconfig.json\nagent/src\nagent/src/tools\nagent/src/tools/executor.ts\nagent/src/tools/metadata-scan.ts\nagent/src/tools/registry.ts\nagent/src/tools/approvals.ts\nagent/src/workflows\nagent/src/workflows/eligibility-check.ts\nagent/src/agent\nagent/src/agent/identity.ts\nagent/src/agent/context-size.ts\nagent/src/agent/loop.ts\nagent/src/agent/budget.ts\nagent/src/agent/classifier.ts\nagent/src/integrations\nagent/src/integrations/sms.ts\nagent/src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts\nagent/src/integrations/payments.ts\nagent/src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.t